      "coverage": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with approximate thermal size: 81.39 km effective diameter (catalog ±0.93 km; additional shape and thermal-model uncertainty). Thermal size is used as a volume-scale approximation. An alternative pole remains possible. The grid marks unavailable imagery; rotational phase is illustrative. The physical size is approximately calibrated by assigning the AKARI thermal effective diameter to the mesh volume-equivalent diameter. Neither source mesh nor spin is modified. Convex inversion supplies only broad outline; no resolved craters, concavities, reflectance or regolith texture can be inferred. Ďurech2020 TableA.2 reports203 cyan plus122 orange ATLAS observations and two poles. The table marks period recovery E (ellipsoid search); that is not evidence of high shape accuracy. The archived convex mesh is retained only as a coarse inverse model.",
